1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,664
Welcome to Atomic Education.

2
00:00:02,723 --> 00:00:09,913
This lesson was written by the Atomic teaching team to help you learn Cambridge Lower Secondary Science with confidence.

3
00:00:09,913 --> 00:00:10,626
Let's begin!

4
00:00:11,685 --> 00:00:14,181
Welcome to Unit 6: Displacement Reactions.

5
00:00:15,240 --> 00:00:19,756
Heavy metals like lead, cadmium and mercury are toxic even in tiny amounts.

6
00:00:19,756 --> 00:00:25,876
To clean polluted water, we can add a more reactive metal that pushes the toxic metal out of solution.

7
00:00:25,876 --> 00:00:27,718
That's a displacement reaction!

8
00:00:28,778 --> 00:00:30,204
In a chemical reaction,

9
00:00:30,204 --> 00:00:36,264
the atoms of the reactants rearrange and bond in new ways to form products with different properties.

10
00:00:36,264 --> 00:00:41,493
Here, two hydrogen molecules react with one oxygen molecule to form two water molecules.

11
00:00:42,553 --> 00:00:47,247
A word equation summarises this using names: hydrogen plus oxygen gives water.

12
00:00:47,247 --> 00:00:53,129
Reactants go on the left, products on the right, and the arrow shows the direction of the reaction.

13
00:00:54,189 --> 00:00:59,893
A symbol equation uses chemical symbols and formulae: two H two, plus O two, gives two H two O.

14
00:00:59,893 --> 00:01:02,448
Chemists all over the world understand it,

15
00:01:02,448 --> 00:01:06,726
and the formula of water shows two hydrogen atoms for every oxygen atom.

16
00:01:07,786 --> 00:01:12,836
A coil of magnesium ribbon is put in a crucible with a lid and weighed: 25.24 grams.

17
00:01:12,836 --> 00:01:17,352
It is heated strongly, lifting the lid slightly now and then to let air in.

18
00:01:17,352 --> 00:01:22,700
Predict: after the reaction, will the mass be higher, lower or the same? Pause and decide.

19
00:01:23,759 --> 00:01:27,502
Watch. The magnesium glows brilliant white inside the crucible.

20
00:01:28,562 --> 00:01:33,078
A white powder is left. The crucible and its contents now weigh 25.40 grams.

21
00:01:34,137 --> 00:01:35,444
Explain what you saw.

22
00:01:35,444 --> 00:01:41,683
Magnesium has reacted with oxygen from the air to form magnesium oxide: two Mg plus O two gives two MgO.

23
00:01:41,683 --> 00:01:44,298
The oxygen atoms have joined the magnesium,

24
00:01:44,298 --> 00:01:50,240
so the solid product is heavier than the magnesium we started with. No atoms are made or destroyed.

25
00:01:50,240 --> 00:01:52,557
Pause and explain it in your own words.
